void myFunction();  // Declaration: No definition needed until odr-used.
void myFunction() { /* body */ }  // Definition: Required if odr-used.
// Implementation note: If myFunction() is called or &myFunction is taken, it's odr-used, triggering compiler to emit a symbol reference for linker resolution. In unevaluated contexts (e.g., sizeof(&myFunction)), it's not odr-used, allowing the compiler to skip definition checks.
